<section>
    <h2 class="page-heading">Installation</h2>

    <p>
        <b>Note: </b> It is a requirement that the Blazor Ramp Core <span class="code-span">core-live-region.js</span> script, <span class="code-span">LiveRegionService</span>, and
        associated <span class="code-span">&lt;AnnouncementHistory /&gt;</span> component are added alongside this component’s specific
        requirements (a stylesheet reference in this instance). You do not need to add the BlazorRamp.Core package separately, as BlazorRamp.Core is included as a transitive package, you only need to add the packages that contain the components
        that you wish to use i.e the <b>BlazorRamp.Tabs</b> NuGet package.
    </p>
    <p>
        Please follow the instructions in the <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Class" href="@GlobalValues.Path_Overview_Getting_Started">@GlobalValues.Main_Nav_Section_Heading_About - @GlobalValues.Page_Heading_Overview_Getting_Started</a>
        ensuring that in the <span class="code-span">&lt;head&gt;</span> section you also add the Tabs stylesheet as follows:
    </p>
    <CodeBox CodeBlock="@CodeSnippets.Add_Tabs_Style_Sheet" AriaLabel="Add Tabs stylesheet code block" />

</section>

<section class="code-table">

    <h2 id="tabs-component-parameters" class="code-table__heading">Tabs component (parent) parameters</h2>

    <table aria-labelledby="tabs-component-parameters">

        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th scope="col">Parameter</th>
                <th scope="col">Type</th>
                <th scope="col">Description</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td>ChildContent</td>
                <td>RenderFragment?</td>
                <td>
                    The render fragment used the child content (for each Tab).
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>AriaLabelledBy</td>
                <td>string?</td>
                <td>
                   You can give the Tabs component an accessible name by either providing an ID of an element such 
                    as a heading to use, or by setting the <span class="code-span">AriaLabel</span> paramater.
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>AriaLabel</td>
                <td>string?</td>
                <td>
                    Used for the accessible name if the <span class="code-span">AriaLabelledBy</span> parameter was not provided. 
                    <b>Note:</b> if neither value is provided a default of "Tabs" will be used for the <span class="code-span">aria-label</span> attribute.
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>ActiveTabIndex</td>
                <td>int</td>
                <td>Gets or sets the zero-based index of the active tab. Defaults to 0.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>ActiveTabIndexChanged</td>
                <td>EventCallback&lt;int&gt;</td>
                <td>Event to recieve the active index manually or used for two-way binding for the active index.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>AutoActivatePanel</td>
                <td>bool</td>
                <td>
                    Determines if the tab panels are shown automatically when its associated tab recieves the focus, or has to be
                    activated manually using the space or enter key after recieving the focus. Defauts to true, auto activate.
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>TabIconPosition</td>
                <td>TabIconPosition (enum)</td>
                <td>Determines the location of any optional icon used on Tabs. Defaults to <span class="code-span">TabIconPosition.Left</span></td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>AdditionalAttributes</td>
                <td>Dictionary&lt;string, object&gt;?</td>
                <td>Sets additional attributes applied to the component's root element.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2 id="tab-component-parameters" class="code-table__heading">Tab component (child) parameters</h2>

    <table aria-labelledby="tab-component-parameters">

        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th scope="col">Parameter</th>
                <th scope="col">Type</th>
                <th scope="col">Description</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td>TabPanelContent</td>
                <td>RenderFragment?</td>
                <td>
                    The content for tab panel.
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>TabTitle</td>
                <td>string</td>
                <td>
                    The tab title but also its accessible name. An exception is raised if a value is not provided.
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>PersistContent</td>
                <td>bool</td>
                <td>
                    Determine whether the tab panel content is retained in the DOM when the tab is not active. Defaults to true.
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>SvgIcon</td>
                <td>string?</td>
                <td>
                    Optional, the name of the css svg variable. As its a css variable it must start with a double dash (--).
                    The airplane icon used in the example above has the name --svg-airplane-icon. <br />
                    The details in the :root pseudo-class is: --svg-airplane-icon: url("data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg . . .
                </td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>HasPanelTabIndex</td>
                <td>bool</td>
                <td>
                    Determines whether a <span class="code-span">tabindex=0</span> is added to the tab panel. If the
                    tab panel does not contain focusable elements then this should be set to true, otherwise it
                    can be set to false. The default value is true.
                </td>
            </tr>

        </tbody>
    </table>
</section>
